  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186133881,
      "id": "d42243ea-58fc-53f6-a0b6-f995bf1d697c",
      "title": "Interpreting the Curl of a Vector Field"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "9449a8b4-8ba7-58e9-ae2f-0159f96a50ad",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186133881/assets/2cb4d2162a3fcd3b4337c22dfc66ebf0f7beb36bc7c085c1340d72363c5554d4.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$\n\nII. $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$\n\nIII. $\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the negative $z$-direction.\n\nIV. $F$ is irrotational",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that $F$ represents the velocity field of flowing water. Place a paddlewheel at $P$ with its axis in the $z$-direction. If it rotates, the field has nonzero curl; if it does not, the field has zero curl.\n\nThe arrows turn a paddlewheel counterclockwise. Thus $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$ throughout space, so $F$ is not irrotational. Curl measures local rotation, even when the arrows also spread outward. Wrap the fingers of your right hand in the counterclockwise direction: your thumb points out of the screen, in the positive $z$-direction.\n\nWith that in mind, check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false.\n- Statement II is true.\n- Statement III is false.\n- Statement IV is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "ca906f3e-492e-549c-9f3f-220a96725c54",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "51792e21-cc93-592a-875d-4348ac48f20b",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "I and IV only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "31d2e6d1-6542-56f2-bf08-dd9738deebb0",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "II and IV only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "6dc6d02e-6db2-545a-8b3a-37699f22183a",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "II and III only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "4108a562-c7da-5589-a562-771ad7aae896",
