  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186133881,
      "id": "d42243ea-58fc-53f6-a0b6-f995bf1d697c",
      "title": "Interpreting the Curl of a Vector Field"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "7844aa4e-756a-5a95-9253-51eb462e394f",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186133881/assets/00ba26c6647de800c9222bebf691d1c8b163e5f2552c4f1017aab2780a537103.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$\n\nII. $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$\n\nIII. $F$ is not irrotational\n\nIV. $\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that $F$ represents the velocity field of flowing water. Place a paddlewheel at $P$ with its axis in the $z$-direction. If it rotates, the field has nonzero curl; if it does not, the field has zero curl.\n\nThe arrows produce no local paddlewheel rotation. Thus $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ throughout space. The field is irrotational, and its zero curl points in neither the positive nor the negative $z$-direction.\n\nWith that in mind, check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true.\n- Statement II is false.\n- Statement III is false.\n- Statement IV is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "7dbd32be-fc7d-5f7a-958e-9af6db448881",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "1698ac7c-90f7-5fd2-bee0-425a632d2b48",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "I only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "df53b7a0-b84d-5177-aaac-2d4f291075e4",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "II and IV only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "b7e10d3b-01ff-54db-8bff-c00a6236a53b",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "II and III only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "ae8b3151-99c6-560e-bc55-0c050bf93a0b",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "I and IV only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "9cfaf79c-78cf-5e47-856d-1c21b8a7fe41",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "I and III only"
